Q: Having an issue while testing Async code in JavaScript using Jest JS
A: <p>The problem is that your test finishes before the promise produces the error. To test in <em>Jest</em> using promises you need to return the promise from the test. Doing that will make the test to wait until the promise is completed and the test would fail if the promise rejected.</p>

<p>Simply add a <code>return</code> statement to your test, try this - </p>

<pre><code>return obj.validateEmail("somemail@gmail.com","80867a1cafc7017cd9a9b510c01d1ba7")
 .then(value =&gt; {
       expect(data).toEqual(value);
   })
});
</code></pre>

<p>From the <em>Jest</em> docs -</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Be sure to return the promise - if you omit this return statement, your test will complete before Promise method completes.</p>
</blockquote>

